WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.151
An interpreter architecture represents a program
as data and uses an execution engine to

00:00:05.151 --> 00:00:10.244
advance it. The model distinguishes the
interpreted program, its state and the engine’s

00:00:10.244 --> 00:00:15.629
state. This separation can make an unavailable
machine or language executable on an existing

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:16.156
platform.

00:00:16.156 --> 00:00:21.814
It also introduces responsibility for
instruction semantics, validation and runtime
behavior

00:00:21.814 --> 00:00:25.627
that ordinary direct execution may not expose in
the same way.

00:00:25.656 --> 00:00:30.366
Virtual machines need not be implemented solely
through interpretation. The JVM

00:00:30.366 --> 00:00:35.553
specification defines an abstract machine
without requiring a particular implementation

00:00:35.553 --> 00:00:40.740
technique; compilation and hybrid execution are
possible. The deck’s Java and compiler-

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.212
bootstrap examples connect runtime organization
to build-time architecture.

00:00:45.212 --> 00:00:50.215
Portability depends on the specified abstraction
and compatible implementations, while

00:00:50.215 --> 00:00:55.218
performance depends on execution strategy and
workload. Treat specific implementation-

00:00:55.218 --> 00:01:00.511
version statements as historical examples unless
they have been rechecked. Does running JVM

00:01:00.511 --> 00:01:04.409
bytecode imply that every instruction is
interpreted one at a time?

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:10.477
No. The specification permits different
implementation technologies, including
compilation.

00:01:10.477 --> 00:01:16.004
A process-control architecture aims to keep a
controlled variable near a desired set point.

00:01:16.004 --> 00:01:21.045
Sensors measure relevant variables, and a
controller chooses changes to manipulated

00:01:21.045 --> 00:01:26.450
variables. Cruise control provides a concrete
vocabulary: desired speed is the set point,

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.791
measured speed is feedback and throttle is
manipulated.

00:01:29.977 --> 00:01:34.816
These roles describe the causal relationship,
not merely a chain of function calls.

00:01:34.977 --> 00:01:39.942
Feedback adjusts actions using observed results;
open-loop control does not use the

00:01:39.942 --> 00:01:44.968
controlled output to correct its action. An
open-loop approach may be adequate under

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:50.352
predictable conditions, while disturbances make
feedback valuable. A software architecture

00:01:50.352 --> 00:01:55.677
must also consider measurement delay, failure
and actuator limits, even if a simple block

00:01:55.677 --> 00:01:56.813
diagram omits them.

00:01:56.977 --> 00:02:02.180
Preserve the distinction between an explanatory
teaching model and a design validated for a

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:06.927
safety-critical application. If a heater follows
a fixed schedule without measuring

00:02:06.927 --> 00:02:12.188
temperature, is it closed-loop temperature
control? No. Without feedback from the
controlled

00:02:12.188 --> 00:02:14.589
variable, it is open loop for temperature.

00:02:14.589 --> 00:02:19.498
Client–server organization gives one component a
requesting role and another a service-

00:02:19.498 --> 00:02:24.632
providing role in an interaction. A file server
supplies files, while a database server can

00:02:24.632 --> 00:02:28.299
execute queries near the stored data and return
selected results.

00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:33.688
Remote communication makes message meaning,
latency, availability and discovery part of the

00:02:33.688 --> 00:02:38.604
design. One component may act as server for one
interaction and client for another.

00:02:38.799 --> 00:02:43.768
Centralizing a service can simplify management
and allow heterogeneous clients, but

00:02:43.768 --> 00:02:48.916
horizontal scaling depends on state,
coordination and routing. Query processing at
the

00:02:48.916 --> 00:02:54.364
server may reduce transfer for selective
queries; it does not guarantee small responses
for

00:02:54.364 --> 00:02:55.262
every workload.

00:02:55.299 --> 00:03:00.516
Location transparency can simplify interfaces
without removing network failure. Explain

00:03:00.516 --> 00:03:05.974
timeout, retry and authorization
responsibilities alongside the boxes so the
design remains

00:03:05.974 --> 00:03:11.491
meaningful when a service is slow or
unavailable. Is a remote database query
equivalent to a

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:14.190
local procedure call in its failure behavior?

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:19.949
No. Communication failures and ambiguous
outcomes require explicit timeout, retry and

00:03:19.949 --> 00:03:21.411
consistency reasoning.

00:03:21.411 --> 00:03:26.570
Peer-to-peer systems distribute service roles
among participants rather than assigning all

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:31.786
work to one permanent server. Peers can both
request and provide data, and the overlay need

00:03:31.786 --> 00:03:36.887
not connect everyone directly. BitTorrent
distributes pieces among participants, allowing

00:03:36.887 --> 00:03:41.244
downloaders to contribute verified pieces before
completing the entire file.

00:03:41.411 --> 00:03:46.993
A complete participant can continue serving as a
seed, but partial participation is already

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:47.422
useful.

00:03:47.422 --> 00:03:52.885
Decentralized data transfer does not imply the
absence of centralized discovery or bootstrap

00:03:52.885 --> 00:03:58.230
dependencies. The source’s original Napster
characterization should be treated as a hybrid

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:03.634
example rather than a proof of fully
decentralized control. Availability and privacy
depend

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:07.196
on the actual protocol, peer behavior and
metadata exposure.

00:04:07.422 --> 00:04:12.556
Networks can partition, peers can disappear and
discovery can fail, so assess resilience

00:04:12.556 --> 00:04:17.691
from concrete replication and routing mechanisms
rather than from the peer-to-peer label

00:04:17.691 --> 00:04:22.884
alone. Must a BitTorrent participant finish the
entire file before uploading useful data?

00:04:22.922 --> 00:04:28.210
No. The protocol allows peers to exchange
available pieces while downloads are still in

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:28.758
progress.
